[{"id":"VRCE-1-63-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":1,"english":"O Rambha, this mighty service you will have to perform in the interest of the celestials, even to take Kausika with the witchery of love.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48aad0f1fa4680cb6f3434b857cf0a371f2fc940ad982a296c2d1f290fa1d56d","compact":"a45be0a203e2c66ea6b2479817491a6b57fd241224c9c34439726775bee7c25b","nasal":"bc3367cd3dc180b4e15e6bb32f38c506f1658b672448c5d0e6dc218c1cd1ed26"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":2,"english":"Thus addressed by the intelligent thousandeyed deity, the Apsarā, O Rāma, with clasped palms, thus bashfully answered the chief of the celestials,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b58721513772c869396d46c5c8c4cdd7f6f46d0ab500f709c75c9d0cdf91e9f","compact":"9add5dd283b8808a39150184c47e0cc807daf36cef76587210e777fd1fb6c62f","nasal":"627d1a773148934024786f85b639e4a215f9b2e5d0edcca70d9c07321e2afac5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":3,"english":"O lord of the celestials, this mighty ascetic, Viśvāmitra, is a terrible person; and, without doubt, he will, O divine one, waxing wroth, curse me. And O god, even this is my fear, and therefore it behove you to favour me. Thus apprehensively addressed by her in fear, the thousand-eyed one answered that damsel trembling and staying with clasped hands, 'Never fear, O Rambhā, good to you! Do you perform my bidding.'","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.663,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-3","DUTT-1-64-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8486a9b5909d199a705d86204c455ed683f04c43ec91f43e694db0bc01ff7228","compact":"6075ba70b5646b057d97070c84f5178880e7213f57c1d4ceec4e9963eba5ff7e","nasal":"6075ba70b5646b057d97070c84f5178880e7213f57c1d4ceec4e9963eba5ff7e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":4,"english":"And O god, even this is my fear, and therefore it behove you to favour me. Thus apprehensively addressed by her in fear, the thousand-eyed one answered that damsel trembling and staying with clasped hands, 'Never fear, O Rambhā, good to you! Do you perform my bidding.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a43222d87ed942a8e6147418f6af22ff0fbe16a2cdfe164da8b03bdbc18f963a","compact":"c66105128ee45902678b818ef8385789c07e5c23df8f80eff366a9a2c00a0a35","nasal":"114e86492f352cf140357366e815f9dd83bbe295db38f3b569138f1e59625447"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":5,"english":"Assuming the form of a Cole, captivating the heart, I will in this spring crowned with graceful trees, stay by your side in company with Kandarpa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9585cf1d1d875fc0d11def54551e867a2dcb82581d762098cd8a411611152fa7","compact":"93482e064f46e4cefba47bf572c54e0f41a97ba5552d933171f862277978d236","nasal":"d1ee5141466e0ce60dcdb693a5d1a3585f5d81711d78727ecbbb75ce0d46186d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":6,"english":"Do you adding to your beauty, diverse blandishments bewitch this ascetic, Kusika's son, O gentle one?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9ceb65fc0e2a03c183dfe5388e853e7fc0fb4b27b20b1e5a3e3211aabd48ae2","compact":"1f216c921f24ba5bb3d4e7470ba0105df13c4fb08f206ec19a2f54a31af8a027","nasal":"c1dcc25a8bc317e6ad8fb5cfa5aab425ee6f258b2c9c0d433b6031335493bdc6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":7,"english":"Hearing Indra's words, that comely damsel of luminous smiles, heightening her charms exceedingly inspired Viśvāmitra with desire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d82792cace9ea6a3a190c76cbc241779869d38ae92c3844fad9e8947ed788fe","compact":"b41c4329e29317ceb4674c56251cf7f86068899ab6d4423ebd4abcd35b0e588d","nasal":"b41c4329e29317ceb4674c56251cf7f86068899ab6d4423ebd4abcd35b0e588d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":8,"english":"He listened to the mellifluous strains of the Cole; and with a delighted heart, he beheld the fair one.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.638,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5e2b678d4f13d37d2417ca5f251cb860781142ecfe24ca9e0727efd1f948cb2","compact":"140ab1d38b6b7382855e3c4c2e3b450b56f5afd78fb6215ee9d2c7f1ee53eb72","nasal":"140ab1d38b6b7382855e3c4c2e3b450b56f5afd78fb6215ee9d2c7f1ee53eb72"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":9,"english":"Anon, listening to the warbling of the Cole and her own incomparable singing, as well as beholding Rambha, the ascetic began to entertain doubts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2838304ebbc015b8a139e938018b81449775458c2900e126288782a6d7461fee","compact":"c88feaf6d38ed1fb7fe0b29171258db618d79e0b3b453b32a85f6f2e930d85c5","nasal":"833678311d0b1e3e2048fb163c0ca04e9bf52b4aab093772216f3cf9a2f85123"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":10,"english":"And knowing for certain that it was the thousand-eyed deity who had devised all that, that foremost of anchorets, Kusika's son, overwhelmed with anger, cursed Rambha, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5f40abaa90672fe385ed6b858a4d65c8243fd8ee8d3fb2a5a123cd6ad6bf97c","compact":"4ba70854b8b38e7a96526ef9876ecaff63739cafd37ab715b01621e58887e125","nasal":"89bb2534e3d2859095c63290c2086b0c333d6ea32a3a204d338f73db6b41b741"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":11,"english":"Since, O Rambhā, you endeavour to seduce me who is bent upon subduing his anger and lust, you shall, O luckless one, remain as a stone for ten thousand years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5f7500918a985e48d496cc08dbe7e4da86b2e5b3ad2dfa9f3af5565fb24e989","compact":"2bacc00d6b1de4802cef006d243501a4e5393e8ee1fee4e94b2ecf8798047970","nasal":"95b7ebd31cecf429e70628da11fe0dcf901b799a95b91a97e363b736aed092b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":12,"english":"And a highly energetic Brāhmaṇa equipped with ascetic energy, will, O Rambha, deliver you, stained because of my ire.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.939,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ae25913225690e0c428fcb54cf3451ee0bdd0a86f1b2c142772483fd6391863","compact":"1a2b09084a2c27c057a46d14fddd7682ccea9dc74e706740844911b22c8b6769","nasal":"b3487f1ca12881528ddf3c01ad0928e3215703e9c5e1d7ab4871aeb2a9c776df"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":13,"english":"Thus said that exceedingly energetic and mighty ascetic Viśvāmitra, unable to contain his anger and indignation of heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.951,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"017f25c47d9e1808a3e9eb069fc579659aab33825cfe8ea36f323c99ea761564","compact":"0e9535f31591aec0c2b95821f0880a14274924db095ca8cddd2a01d1231861fa","nasal":"188aa575b53f2dd754d6f080166352fd12816d9d054f1464da52348083261cc1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":14,"english":"And in consequence of his mighty curse, Rambha was turned into a stone. Hearing the curse of the mighty saint, both Kandarpa and Indra left the place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80edb6b1cb3eb123f81bb4df16ed74f6672b6ecf63f142a61c36203aca161d17","compact":"3dff8d40ca443b01400fd7e297ca5a40479a593b45711386d5ccbd05aa7efb3d","nasal":"8c6fa8b36ca1c0ba43c02b5efb75228f098b429d09006c010103052bcf61f276"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-63-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":63,"verse":15,"english":"O Rāma, on account of his anger, and his sense remaining still unsubdued he found no rest from deterioration of ascetic merit. And coming by decrease of ascetic merit, he thought within himself, ‘No more shall I suffer anger to exercise me, nor will I ever say anything to any.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.982,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-64-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1063015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e43cd646a0aff6340d7c18e36ee9ffba100d0cc05e1c15b5be92a9e61484bcfe","compact":"9a2a1fc826490b651dbfd03cfaf5a6e02a74d7c2b1a04e9360fa84d4118dcc47","nasal":"8f78bf4d598899ff8d9f65f3a5d463c9affdb9910ca97227abd353d8cc38c294"}}]
